rota lap 4360, row 0 was Aether and my elder lap read it, so advanced by hand to row 1 -- Air, the row that feels; read foundations/20260826-021732_air-the-row-that-feels.md, and its teaching chose the lap: walk the fence line and press each post, and where the hand passes through the boundary was a wish
think Three guards were widened this week to derive their population from tools/fixtures/t/tame_style_rooms.txt rather than from an inline list. That is the right move and it leaves one question standing: the roster file is itself a hand-written list of twenty rooms, and nothing measures what it leaves out.
think Pressed on it. git ls-files over authored .rye, minus symlinks and .cache/ and bin/, reads 1,729 files; 1,127 stand under a roster room and 551 do not. lotus/ alone holds 238, larger than most rooms on the list.
think The roster's own head already names a twenty-first room, rye/tests, and declines to add it -- deliberately, with reasons. It sizes that deferred lap from the camelCase advisory ratchet: seven names, six after an inherited-name exemption.
think So I read the other half. The bans FAIL parity rather than printing a count, and nobody had run them over the rooms this file omits. 736 hits across 113 files, zero inside a comment: 718 std.debug.assert( in rye/tests, twelve copyForwards and six copyBackwards in the three tests named for those primitives. The deferral was sound and its stated size was three orders short, because the number that sized it came from the half of the law that only advises.
think Checked provenance before claiming it. rye/tests is this tree's own -- mantra_weave_test.rye, tally_gardens_test.rye, ed25519_sign_test.rye -- rather than inherited Zig std, so the law reaches it and makes no test exemption.
obs Wrote tools/fixtures/t/tame_reach_scan.sh: population from git ls-files rather than find, because the bans half's find flags pointed tree-wide would sweep vendor/ and every build leftover, and tracked is what a clone receives. One gate at zero, phantom_rooms -- a roster line naming no tracked Rye, which is this whole subject wearing its smallest form. Two ratchets under ceilings that only fall, 551 and 736. tools/fixtures/ is read past because a guard proves its refusals by planting them.
obs I report rather than decide. Whether rye/tests joins the roster moves five ratchet ceilings at once and is the owning hand's lap; what this meter buys is that the hand sizes it from a measurement.
obs Against myself, twice. I opened the cold roster pass before fleet_round_open.sh, so it measured a tree three commits behind xy and carried fold_shelf_link_repoint red -- a fault upstream had already repaired in cb710cb65. Stopped it with tools/f/fleet_call.sh --pattern standing_equipment_run --signal TERM, which refused twelve peer processes by name and sent to exactly one, then adopted 813bc2066d and re-ran. And I copied the scan into tools/fixtures/ while the first pass was still running, against hold still; removed it before that run finished.
obs The pin refused a fifth ship today. construction/REDS.md stands at 40,727 of 40,960, so this row is cited by stamp, 20260908.192416, unbooked. construction/ITINERARY.md fits at 40,959 of 40,960 -- one byte of headroom, after five passes of trimming my own account.
